	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c27db6fbad819908","type":"text","text":"# De que se compone\nEl sistema inmunologico se compone de\n1. Vasos Linfaticos\n2. Organos Linfoides\n\t* Medula Osea\n\t* Nodulos Linfaticos\n\t\t* Amigdalas\n\t* Bazo\n\t* Timo\n3. Monocitos: (Monos $\\equiv$ Solo en Griego) (Citos $\\equiv$ Celula en Griego)\n4. Linfocitos (Lympha $\\equiv$ Agua en Griego)\n\n","x":-125,"y":-30,"width":405,"height":270},
		{"id":"e35e3f2216e0d147","type":"text","text":"# De que se compone\nEl sistema inmunologico se compone de\n1. Vasos Linfaticos\n2. Organos Linfoides\n\t* Medula Osea\n\t* Nodulos Linfaticos\n\t\t* Amigdalas\n\t* Bazo\n\t* Timo\n3. Monocitos: (Monos $\\equiv$ Solo en Griego) (Citos $\\equiv$ Celula en Griego)\n4. Linfocitos (Lympha $\\equiv$ Agua en Griego)\n\n","x":-125,"y":-30,"width":405,"height":270},
		{"id":"645927745b1caf20","type":"text","text":"# Antibodies\nThese are proteins made by specific white blood cells\n# Pathogen and Antigens\nPathogens are microbes which invade the body and cause illness. The antigens are parts of the pathogen which the body identifies to alert the body of infection.\n# The B Lymphocyte\nThese are part of the adaptive immune system, and they help deal with \n1. bacterias which are foreign\n2. Toxins\n3. Protozoa\n4. Viruses\n","x":-327,"y":620,"width":405,"height":250},
		{"id":"529334deb96733dd","type":"text","text":"# Barriers\nThese are part of the nonspecific immune system. These are composed of things like\n1. Your skin\n2. Mucus\n3. Gastric Acid\n# Innate Defenses\n## <mark style=\"background: #CACFD9A6;\">Phagocytes</mark>\nThese are white blood cells whose purpose is to eat intruders.\n### <mark style=\"background: #CACFD9A6;\">Neutrophils</mark>\nThe most abundant white blood cell, which will self destruct after eating a pathogen.\n### <mark style=\"background: #CACFD9A6;\">Macrophages</mark>\nThey grab pathogens through their cytoplasmic extensions (which are like tentacles), engulfs and digests them. They can repeatedly do this\n### <mark style=\"background: #CACFD9A6;\">NK Cells (Natural Killer)</mark>\nThese look for cells which are infected by viruses or have become cancerous. These cells induce [[Parts of a Cell#Lysosome|apoptosis]] by injecting an enzyme into the cell.","x":-327,"y":340,"width":405,"height":250},
		{"id":"544dc87df53c1daf","type":"text","text":"# <mark style=\"background: #CACFD9A6;\">White Blood Cells</mark>\n","x":-600,"y":40,"width":405,"height":250}
	],
	"edges":[]
